{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeGGKnYt7jzA9Zpm8JVhk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Root Cause\n\nThe failure is **not** in `routes/public.map` (which correctly maps `/health` → `health`, listed before the `/*` wildcard entry). It's a source-level bug in `router/routes.go`:\n\n```go\nfunc HealthHandler() string { return \"wildcard\" }\n```\n\n`HealthHandler()` is hardcoded to return `\"wildcard\"` instead of `\"health\"`. This makes it look as if the `/health` route is being shadowed by the wildcard `/*` route, but in reality the route map is fine — the handler function itself simply returns the wrong string literal.\n\n**Fix location:** `router/routes.go`, change the return value from `\"wildcard\"` to `\"health\"`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":203,"cache_read_input_tokens":4113,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":203},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e2805595-c26a-456c-a426-270c38a53f29","uuid":"ba4afd80-4500-4fea-84f7-e635c9b05436","timestamp":"2026-08-21T17:10:51.866Z","request_id":"req_011CeGGKmbqH2t18VEcBmrDw"}
